wm2tj (0.1.0~beta3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * wm2tj: keep the stacking order across a restart (SIGHUP). Windows were
    released in reverse creation order, which turned the stack over on
    every restart and could leave a settings window under the others.
  * wm2tj-favorites, wm2tj-bar: do not rebuild the menu and restart wm2tj
    themselves while wm2-menu-sync.path (systemd --user) watches the
    favourites file, so a change restarts wm2tj once instead of twice.
  * wm2tj-favorites: drop the raise after the restart (it had no effect);
    a hand-written comment after "new_label none" is no longer taken for
    the entry's name.

 -- tetsu <wm2tj@biz.kaie-net.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:48:17 +0900

wm2tj (0.1.0~beta2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * wm2tj-favorites: changes stay in the window until Apply (with Revert,
    and a question when closing with changes not applied), so wm2tj is
    restarted once per Apply instead of on every add, remove or move; the
    application list is updated in place instead of rebuilt; the window
    is raised again after wm2tj restarts.

 -- tetsu <wm2tj@biz.kaie-net.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:37:10 +0900

